      "_uid": "f69f3eab-2d1b-4862-84b6-5c2b7336a838",
      "text_markdown": "From girdle checks at stewardess college to golden wings after fifty years in the cabin, one American Airlines family carries the 747 rollout, 9/11, sobriety, and loss across three generations.\n\nRobyn Stewart has flown for American Airlines since 1971. Her son Caleb directed the film. Jay R. Ricks, her father, was an AA flight engineer on the 747 training program. Jock Bethune, an AA media production specialist, appears on camera.",
